WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.100
-Thank you, everybody.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.734
Welcome, welcome, welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.534
You're here. You're watching. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:07.901
Thank you very much for tuning in.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.501
Guys, let's get to some news.

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:12.067
Today, President Biden held a meeting at the White House

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:14.934
with Israeli President Isaac Herzog.

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:17.000
Biden and Israel's president spent hours together.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.934
They discussed Iran, Russia,

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:21.734
and all of their favorite tracks off the new Taylor Swift album.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.767
"Lavender Haze."

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:27.033
Meanwhile, earlier today, President Biden also announced

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:30.167
a plan to cut hidden bank and credit-card fees

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:33.334
in an effort to give families more breathing room.

00:00:33.334 --> 00:00:34.601
Yeah.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.501
[ Cheers and applause ] Good.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.033
More breathing room. Interesting. Yeah.

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.367
"Breathing room" sounds like

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:42.767
Biden's launching his own line of Skims.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:44.334
To be honest, I don't know if Biden

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:46.834
is the best person to talk about giving people breathing room.

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:48.734
But I don't know. Maybe I'm wrong. I don't know.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:51.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:55.934
Biden also said that he's looking to get rid of

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:58.534
added fees on cable bills.

00:00:58.534 --> 00:01:00.234
That's great news.

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:03.400
[ Cheers and applause ] That's great news.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.367
Great news for the three people who still have cable.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:06.901
It's amazing news.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:10.033
Some more news -- Russia just notified the U.S.

00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:13.000
that they would be launching nuclear-capable missiles

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.934
as part of their annual nuclear exercise.

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:16.133
Russia is just like us --

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.133
they also exercise only once a year.

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:19.400
It's great.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.434
But the U.S. is keeping a close eye on Russia.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:23.167
Yesterday, Biden said that it would be

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:24.968
a "serious, serious mistake"

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:27.234
for Russia to use nuclear weapons.

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:30.167
Wow. I haven't heard words that powerful

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.701
since FDR called Japan's attack on Pearl Harbor

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:35.133
a "major no-no." [ Laughter ]

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:38.334
That's right. Biden said that if Russia uses nuclear weapons

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:41.767
they would be making a "serious, serious mistake."

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.267
Yep. And he didn't stop there.

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:46.868
Next he said, "For realsies, you better not."

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:48.367
-Wow.

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:50.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:51.901
-No. He went on. -Oh.

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.467
[ Applause ]

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.567
-"For realsies." -Yeah.

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.767
-He went on to say, "But if you wanna really be real,

00:01:57.767 --> 00:01:59.067
I'm actually on BeReal.

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:01.300
Just search POTUS and check it out."

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.801
And finally, he said, "But seriously, no cap fam.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.601
This behavior is making me salty. Don't @ me."

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:08.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.968
What is he talk-- I don't know what he's doing.

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:13.968
Guys, I want to say happy birthday to Hillary Clinton,

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:16.133
who turned 75 today.

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:17.934
[ Applause ]

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:19.734
Hillary Clinton.

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:22.133
Of course, Hillary got a lot of texts for her birthday,

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:23.868
and we actually got ahold of some of them.

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:26.033
Yeah, for instance, Ron DeSantis texted...

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.601
Next, Vladimir Putin texted...

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.834
Then Adidas texted...

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.801
"We're giving them away. Free."

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.968
Next up, Donald Trump texted...

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:56.167
Bernie Sanders texted...

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:05.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:07.167
[As Sanders] Send!

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:09.133
[ Applause ]

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:12.000
Next up, Bill Clinton texted...

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.501
That's nice.

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:15.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:18.000
That's nice.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.868
And finally, Joe Biden texted...

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:27.901
"Send!"

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:29.300
[ Applause ]

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:32.567
Nice of everyone to reach out, don't you think?

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:35.400
That's right. Today is Hillary Clinton's 75th birthday.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.367
But I looked it up, and it turns out October 26th

00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:38.767
is a lot of people's birthday,

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:40.868
so it's only fair that I wish them all a happy birthday.

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:42.267
This should only take a second.

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:43.868
Feel free to sing along if you want.

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:45.367
[ Clears throat ]

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:48.100
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:51.067
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:55.367
♪ Happy birthday, dear Hillary Clinton ♪

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:58.167
♪ And Keith Urban ♪

00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.901
♪ And Seth MacFarlane ♪

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:03.467
♪ And Pat Sajak ♪

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:07.200
♪ And John Heder, a.k.a. Napoleon Dynamite ♪

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.834
♪ And Rita Wilson ♪

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:12.300
♪ And Dylan McDermott ♪

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.901
♪ And Jaclyn Smith ♪

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:16.434
[ Clock ticking ]

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:18.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:21.400
♪ And Bootsy Collins ♪

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.834
♪ And Schoolboy Q ♪

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:28.968
♪ And my childhood babysitter, Tiffany O'Brien ♪

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:32.267
[ Clock ticking ]

00:04:32.267 --> 00:04:36.467
♪ And professional wrestler C.M. Punk ♪

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:39.767
♪ And former Kenyan President Uhuru Kenyatta ♪

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:41.167
Oh, forget it. I can't do everybody.

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:46.267
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:50.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:52.534
-Well, you forgot to mention

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:55.234
that today is my birthday, Jimmy.

00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:57.434
-Well, we got a lot of jokes to tell.

00:04:57.434 --> 00:04:59.267
Guys --

00:04:59.267 --> 00:05:00.734
[ Audience awws ]

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:03.734
Some business -- Some business news.

00:05:03.734 --> 00:05:05.667
Today TJ Maxx announced

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.734
that they were cutting ties with Kanye West

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:10.601
and no longer selling any of his Yeezy merchandise.

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:12.734
And -- And I personally think I had a small part in that.

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:14.701
Here's a joke that we did from the monologue last night.

00:05:14.701 --> 00:05:15.901
This is real.

00:05:15.901 --> 00:05:17.801
And now GAP also announced

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:20.200
that they're pulling all Yeezy products from their stores.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.667
-Oh. Meanwhile, TJ Maxx is like,

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:24.934
"We'll sell whatever ya got.

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:27.701
We let it rip in this place."

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:30.000
Thank you for watching, TJ Maxx.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.901
We love you guys.

00:05:32.901 --> 00:05:35.000
-You're a Maxxanista. -Yeah.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.334
Get this, everyone.

00:05:36.334 --> 00:05:38.400
Snoop Dogg's professional blunt roller

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.901
just revealed that Snoop smokes up to 150 blunts a day.

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:44.534
You know, I'm worried

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:46.601
because if this keeps up, he might form a habit.

00:05:46.601 --> 00:05:48.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:50.200
Guys, I heard about a documentary

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.200
about Ed Sheeran in the works. I love Ed Sheeran.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:55.901
It sounds cool, but I'm not sure the producers

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:57.100
really did their research.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.801
Take a look at the promo they released.

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:00.734
-We're excited to announce a documentary

00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:04.033
about one of the world's biggest music stars, Ed Sheeran.

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:05.934
We'll dive into Ed Sheeran's life,

00:06:05.934 --> 00:06:08.801
his dedication to music, his hobbies and interests,

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.834
and we'll look at never-before-seen photos

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:13.467
of the legendary musician at home and on the road.

00:06:13.467 --> 00:06:16.267
"The Ed Sheeran Documentary." Don't miss it.

00:06:16.267 --> 00:06:18.100
-You see what I mean? I just feel like --

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.834
I feel like they didn't do their homework.

00:06:20.834 --> 00:06:23.434
[ Applause ]

00:06:23.434 --> 00:06:25.934
Hey, I saw that the new horror series "The Watcher"

00:06:25.934 --> 00:06:27.667
is the number-one show on Netflix

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:29.300
for the second week in a row.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:30.601 --> 00:06:33.300
Over 270 million hours viewed since its release.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:35.367
-Wait. Did you say "The Watcher"?

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:38.300
-Yeah. Why? -Well, that's what the guy

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:41.534
who wrote us that letter called himself.

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:43.501
-What letter? -This one.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:47.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:52.501
-"Dearest neighbor at Studio 6B,

00:06:52.501 --> 00:06:54.133
allow me to welcome you to the building.

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:57.334
I've been put in charge of watching you.

00:06:57.334 --> 00:06:59.634
This message will not be the last.

00:06:59.634 --> 00:07:04.934
Your studio is my obsession, and now you are, too.

00:07:04.934 --> 00:07:07.334
Who am I? I am the Watcher.

00:07:07.334 --> 00:07:09.534
I will never stop watching."

00:07:09.534 --> 00:07:11.467
[ Eerie music plays ]

00:07:11.467 --> 00:07:13.734
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.067 --> 00:07:18.000
That's so nice of you!

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.133
-[ Giggles ] Thanks, Jimmy. I'm a really big fan.

00:07:21.133 --> 00:07:23.501
-Oh, nice to see you.

00:07:23.501 --> 00:07:25.334
[ Applause ]

00:07:25.334 --> 00:07:29.534
He watches. He watches the show.

00:07:29.534 --> 00:07:30.968
-That's the Watcher. -Here you go.

00:07:30.968 --> 00:07:32.567
-Thank you. Yeah, throw the letter back.

00:07:32.567 --> 00:07:33.834
-No problem.

00:07:33.834 --> 00:07:36.534
-Oh. Got it. -Yeah. I got it. No problem.

00:07:36.534 --> 00:07:37.901
Some more, uh...

00:07:37.901 --> 00:07:41.400
[ Applause ]

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:43.334
Some more entertainment news. Next week, "Jeopardy!"

00:07:43.334 --> 00:07:45.901
is bringing back its "Tournament of Champions" where --

00:07:45.901 --> 00:07:47.367
I love it.

00:07:47.367 --> 00:07:49.534
Where the year's best contestants

00:07:49.534 --> 00:07:51.300
face off against each other.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:52.868
Yeah, I saw a commercial for it last night.

00:07:52.868 --> 00:07:54.000
It doesn't look like they picked

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.367
the best of the best for it, though.

00:07:55.367 --> 00:07:57.033
I don't know. You guys be the judge.

00:07:57.033 --> 00:08:00.834
-This is "Jeopardy!'s Tournament of Champions."

00:08:05.601 --> 00:08:06.834
-Elizabeth. -What is "Fight Club"?

00:08:06.834 --> 00:08:08.234
-No.

00:08:14.067 --> 00:08:15.801
Suzanne. -Who is Billy Crystal?

00:08:15.801 --> 00:08:17.100
-No.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.767
Here is a pair of wireless these with a friendly name.

00:08:19.767 --> 00:08:21.133
Fernando. -What are plants?

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:22.300
-No. Chris?

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:23.868
-What is cheddar cheese? -No.

00:08:30.934 --> 00:08:32.501
Tory. -Who are the Wright Brothers?

00:08:32.501 --> 00:08:33.901
-No.

00:08:37.467 --> 00:08:39.000
Rhiannon. -What is "Cake Boss"?

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.601
-No.

00:08:45.801 --> 00:08:48.234
-What's a dab? -No.

00:08:48.234 --> 00:08:51.634
-Ah. Interesting.

00:08:51.634 --> 00:08:53.901
Right? That's interesting.

00:08:53.901 --> 00:08:55.367
Well, this is going viral.

00:08:55.367 --> 00:08:57.501
An antique furniture gallery showed off a rare

00:08:57.501 --> 00:09:00.400
19th-century Italian desk. This is real.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.868
An Italian desk. And it's got a lot of storage space.

00:09:02.868 --> 00:09:04.200
Look at this thing.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.367
-First we have here is you press a button,

00:09:06.367 --> 00:09:07.834
and the writing slope comes out.

00:09:07.834 --> 00:09:10.567
Then, on the sides, you press one of the buttons,

00:09:10.567 --> 00:09:12.133
and a secret drawer comes out.

00:09:12.133 --> 00:09:14.434
You press another button on the inside,

00:09:14.434 --> 00:09:16.300
and secret drawers come out on the end.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:19.601
Press a button on the side, the lion heads come out.

00:09:19.601 --> 00:09:22.234
And then you press a button further here,

00:09:22.234 --> 00:09:23.934
and two more drawers come out.

00:09:23.934 --> 00:09:26.667
Another drawer at the top.

00:09:26.667 --> 00:09:28.968
Press a button, more drawers.

00:09:28.968 --> 00:09:31.601
And then you press another button, and another one.

00:09:31.601 --> 00:09:33.734
And here's the centerpiece for this one,

00:09:33.734 --> 00:09:36.000
where you open it up, the drawers come out.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.567
Of course, these are secret.

00:09:37.567 --> 00:09:39.934
[ Laughter ]

00:09:39.934 --> 00:09:41.133
-I'm sorry.

00:09:41.133 --> 00:09:43.100
That's when you know you got a weed problem.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.734
You know what I'm saying?

00:09:44.734 --> 00:09:46.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:50.667 --> 00:09:53.033
Update on the story -- Snoop Dogg just moved to Italy.

00:09:53.033 --> 00:09:55.000
-Are you serious? -Yep.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.601
The desk also comes with a placard that says...

00:10:00.067 --> 00:10:02.601
Well, there's a lot of bad things going on in the news right now,

00:10:02.601 --> 00:10:04.968
but it looks like they solved at least one pressing issue.

00:10:04.968 --> 00:10:06.434
Watch this. -We'll, you've heard about

00:10:06.434 --> 00:10:09.234
horseshoes, but what about horse sneakers?

00:10:09.234 --> 00:10:11.167
A new company called Horse Kicks

00:10:11.167 --> 00:10:14.634
is now selling high-end sneakers made just for horses.

00:10:14.634 --> 00:10:16.467
You'll find lots of the major brands,

00:10:16.467 --> 00:10:18.701
like New Balance and Nike Air Jordans.

00:10:18.701 --> 00:10:23.300
You can even get your horse sneakers to match your own.

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:26.567
-They have horse sneakers from Nike, New Balance,

00:10:26.567 --> 00:10:28.434
and even those gross toe shoes

00:10:28.434 --> 00:10:31.434
that everyone's embarrassed to wear in public.

00:10:31.434 --> 00:10:35.434
They don't wear them in public. Only at home.

00:10:35.434 --> 00:10:37.734
And finally, Costco is selling

00:10:37.734 --> 00:10:39.901
the world's largest jigsaw puzzle.

00:10:39.901 --> 00:10:45.033
It's 29 feet long, 8 feet tall, and 60,000 pieces.

00:10:45.033 --> 00:10:47.601
Yeah, the bottom left corner goes on your coffee table.

00:10:47.601 --> 00:10:49.801
The bottom right goes in Zimbabwe.

00:10:49.801 --> 00:10:52.234
And a helpful hint. Here's what I did.

00:10:52.234 --> 00:10:54.701
Start by taking seven or eight days to find the corner pieces.

00:10:54.701 --> 00:10:56.801
Yeah. We have a great show, everyone.

